---
import MarketingShell from '../layouts/MarketingShell.astro';
import Footer from '../components/marketing/Footer.astro';
import QuoteBlock from '../components/marketing/QuoteBlock.astro';
import { PageHeader } from '@p31ca/canon-astro';
import { papers } from '../data/p31-research.ts';
import { FLAGSHIP_LIVE_COUNT } from '../data/flagships';
import constants from '../data/p31-mesh-constants.json';
// Phase 3 Batch 1 — canon adoption chain (PAGE-CONTRACTS + phase2 handoff):
// tokens → layers → class recipes → attribute-scoped component CSS.
import '@p31ca/canon/tokens.css';
import '@p31ca/canon/css/layers.css';
import '@p31ca/canon-parts/recipes.css';
import '@p31ca/design-core/css/canon-v2.css';

const publishedCount = papers.length;

const stackDiagram = `
flowchart TB
    classDef core fill:royalblue,stroke:navy,color:white
    classDef infra fill:slategray,stroke:darkslategray,color:white
    classDef external fill:goldenrod,stroke:darkgoldenrod,color:black
    subgraph Edge["Cloudflare edge"]
        W["12 Workers"]:::core
        D["10 D1 databases"]:::infra
        O["16 Durable Objects"]:::infra
    end
    subgraph Tools["Agent surface"]
        M["124 MCP tools<br/>as of 2026-10-13"]:::core
    end
    User["Family member"]:::external --> W
    W --> D
    W --> O
    M --> W
`

const orgTimeline = `
timeline
    title P31 Labs
    2024 : Founded
         : Tetrahedron Protocol published
    2025 : First flagship live
         : Open research on Zenodo
    2026 : 501(c)(3) determination
         : 22 papers on Zenodo
         : Enterprise package v2.0
`
---

<MarketingShell
  title="About — P31 Labs"
  description="Sovereign infrastructure for neurodivergent families, built by a father who needed it. The story of William Johnson, the stack, and the 501(c)(3)."
  theme="rose"
>
  <main id="main-content" class="section">
    <div class="abf6-max-w-4xl abf6-mx-auto abf6-px-6 abf6-md-px-12 abf6-lg-px-16">
      <div class="sh-space-y-4">
        <PageHeader
          title="About"
          subtitle="Sovereign infrastructure for neurodivergent families, built by a father who needed it."
        />
        <div class="sh-h-1 sh-w-16 sh-rounded-full p31-header-bar" style="background: var(--p31-accent);"></div>
      </div>

      <p class="abf6-mt-6 abf6-text-lg abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text);">
        P31 Labs is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit building sovereign AI tools for neurodivergent families. The stack is open source, costs about $5 a month to run, and keeps identity and audit records under your control — not a company's. Everything is verifiable: 22 citable papers, live code, a public registry. This page tells who built it and why.
      </p>

      <div class="abf6-mt-16 abf6-space-y-8">

        {/* ── The world before ── */}
        <section class="glass-card">
          <div class="abf6-p-8 abf6-space-y-6">
            <h2 class="abf6-text-2xl abf6-font-bold" style="color: var(--p31-text);">The problem was the tools</h2>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              When assistive technology is extractive — when your family's data is the product, locked behind corporate walls, dependent on a subscription and a login you don't control — the people who need the tools most are the ones it fails. Neurodivergent families need care infrastructure that is <em>theirs</em>: private by default, sovereign by design, and provable.
            </p>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              None of it existed. So it had to be built.
            </p>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              The same pattern holds at market scale. Worldwide sovereign cloud IaaS spending is forecast at <strong style="color: var(--p31-text);">$80 billion in 2026</strong>, up 35.6% from 2025 (<a href={constants.gartnerSovereignCloudIaaS2026Url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">Gartner press release, Feb 2026</a>) — and it targets governments and enterprises, not households. The family-sized intersection was empty.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── The turn ── */}
        <section class="glass-card">
          <div class="abf6-p-8 abf6-space-y-6">
            <h2 class="abf6-text-2xl abf6-font-bold" style="color: var(--p31-text);">The founder</h2>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              P31 Labs was founded by <strong style="color: var(--p31-text);">William Johnson</strong> — an AuDHD engineer and former DoD civilian. He spent sixteen years as a DoD civilian engineering technician (GS-0802-12) at Trident Refit Facility in Kings Bay, Georgia — work with an uncompromising reliability standard, where a single point of failure is not acceptable. That same ethos is the K4 topology underneath the whole stack: no single point of failure.
            </p>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              He is also a single father to two neurodivergent children. The stack was forged out of household survival during severe medical and legal hardship — stress-tested in a live, multi-adversarial environment, every line of code.
            </p>
            <QuoteBlock
              text="The human mind does not store reality — it constructs it."
              citeName="William R. Johnson, “Consciousness, Memory, and the Architecture of Self-Preservation” (P31 Research Paper III)"
              citeHref="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19416491"
              citeNote="Zenodo DOI · full PDF on the Research page"
            />
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              What started as a personal need became an open-source stack anyone can deploy: a real proof layer — an audit chain you can verify in ninety seconds, post-quantum identity that lives on your device, and research that is open and citable.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── The build ── */}
        <section class="glass-card">
          <div class="abf6-p-8 abf6-space-y-6">
            <h2 class="abf6-text-2xl abf6-font-bold" style="color: var(--p31-text);">The build</h2>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              The whole stack runs on Cloudflare's edge network for about <strong style="color: var(--p31-text);">$5 a month</strong> on the paid plan — zero added server costs, open source, citable on Zenodo. The <a href="/runbook" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">$5 stack runbook</a> spells out the exact arithmetic.
            </p>
            <pre id="about-stack-diagram" class="mermaid" set:html={stackDiagram} />
            <p class="abf6-text-sm" style="color: var(--p31-text-tertiary);">
              <a href={constants.mcpRegistryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">Our live registry</a> lists 44 servers, 22 live, 124 tools (as of 2026-10-13) · {FLAGSHIP_LIVE_COUNT} live flagship surfaces · <a href={constants.zenodoCommunityUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">{publishedCount} DOI-verified papers on Zenodo</a> · EIN 42-1888158
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── The K4 / tetrahedron ── */}
        <section class="glass-card">
          <div class="abf6-p-8 abf6-space-y-6">
            <h2 class="abf6-text-2xl abf6-font-bold" style="color: var(--p31-text);">The geometric anchor</h2>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              The K4 — four vertices, six edges, rigidity 6 — is the minimum isostatic structure. It's the geometric proof that anchors the research: a structure that cannot flex, that is exactly as connected as it needs to be. It's why the dome on this page is a geodesic, and why the research is about families that build.
            </p>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              Read it in <a href="/research" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">The Tetrahedron Protocol</a>, the founding paper.
            </p>
            <QuoteBlock
              text="Just moving the little trim tab builds a low pressure that pulls the rudder around. Takes almost no effort at all. So I said that the little individual can be a trim tab."
              citeName="R. Buckminster Fuller, 1972 Playboy interview"
              citeHref={constants.fullerTrimTabSourceUrl}
              citeNote="quoted in The Marginalian, 2015"
            />
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              That is the K4 idea at human scale — minimum leverage, maximum turn. <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19782991" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">Paper XIV</a> maps Fuller's fifty-year prediction onto the P31 timeline, and <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19783001" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">Paper XX</a> turns the trimtab into a design declaration.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── The org timeline ── */}
        <section class="glass-card">
          <div class="abf6-p-8 abf6-space-y-6">
            <h2 class="abf6-text-2xl abf6-font-bold" style="color: var(--p31-text);">The org timeline</h2>
            <pre class="mermaid" set:html={orgTimeline} />
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── The 501(c)(3) proof ── */}
        <section class="glass-card">
          <div class="abf6-p-8 abf6-space-y-6">
            <h2 class="abf6-text-2xl abf6-font-bold" style="color: var(--p31-text);">The 501(c)(3) proof</h2>
            <div data-p31="grid" data-cols="2" data-even class="abf6-gap-4">
              <div class="abf6-rounded-xl abf6-border abf6-p-5" style="border-color: var(--p31-glass-border); background: var(--p31-panel-surface);">
                <div class="abf6-text-xs abf6-font-semibold abf6-tracking-widest abf6-uppercase" style="color: var(--p31-text-tertiary);">Status</div>
                <div class="abf6-mt-1 abf6-text-lg abf6-font-bold" style="color: var(--p31-text);">501(c)(3)</div>
              </div>
              <div class="abf6-rounded-xl abf6-border abf6-p-5" style="border-color: var(--p31-glass-border); background: var(--p31-panel-surface);">
                <div class="abf6-text-xs abf6-font-semibold abf6-tracking-widest abf6-uppercase" style="color: var(--p31-text-tertiary);">EIN</div>
                <div class="abf6-mt-1 abf6-text-lg abf6-font-bold abf6-font-mono" style="color: var(--p31-text);">42-1888158</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="abf6-text-base abf6-leading-relaxed" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              Donations are tax-deductible to the fullest extent of the law. Research is published on Zenodo under open licenses; code is on GitHub under AGPL.
            </p>
            <h3 class="abf6-text-lg abf6-font-bold abf6-pt-2" style="color: var(--p31-text);">Citable evidence — named references</h3>
            <ul class="abf6-space-y-2 abf6-text-sm" style="color: var(--p31-text-secondary);">
              <li>The Tetrahedron Protocol: A Grand Unified Theory of Structural Resilience — <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19004485" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="abf6-font-mono" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">10.5281/zenodo.19004485</a></li>
              <li>Strategic Convergence of Geometric Security and Cognitive Resilience: P31 Labs Genesis Whitepaper — <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19411363" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="abf6-font-mono" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">10.5281/zenodo.19411363</a></li>
              <li>Paper XII: The Sovereign Stack — <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19782969" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="abf6-font-mono" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">10.5281/zenodo.19782969</a></li>
              <li>Paper III: Consciousness, Memory, and the Architecture of Self-Preservation — <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19416491" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="abf6-font-mono" style="color: var(--p31-accent);">10.5281/zenodo.19416491</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        {/* ── CTA ── */}
        <section class="abf6-text-center abf6-py-10">
          <div class="abf6-flex abf6-flex-wrap abf6-justify-center abf6-gap-4">
            <a href="/team" class="abf6-inline-flex abf6-items-center abf6-gap-2 abf6-rounded-full abf6-px-6 abf6-py-3 abf6-text-sm abf6-font-semibold abf6-transition"
               style="background: var(--p31-accent); color: var(--p31-void);">
              Meet the team
            </a>
            <a href="/research" class="abf6-inline-flex abf6-items-center abf6-gap-2 abf6-rounded-full abf6-px-6 abf6-py-3 abf6-text-sm abf6-font-semibold abf6-transition abf6-border"
               style="border-color: var(--p31-glass-border); color: var(--p31-text);">
              Read the research
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</MarketingShell>